    "extracted text": "The synthesis gel formula is described as: 1 SiO2: 0.05 GeO2: (0–0.04) Al2O3: (0–0.30) R(OH)2: (0–2.56) NH4F: 5 H2O. Crystallization was performed at 453 K (180°C) under static conditions. The structure directing agent (R(OH)2) is hexamethonium dihydroxide. Seeds (5 wt% ITQ-13 with respect to inorganic oxides of SiO2) were added to promote crystallization. The samples were calcined at 623 K for 3h, then raised to 853 K at 1 K/min and kept at this temperature for 3h to remove the organic template.",
    "property mapping": "Si: 1 SiO2 in the gel formula (normalized to 1)\nGe: 0.05 GeO2 in the gel formula\nAl: (0-0.04) Al2O3 in the gel formula, and Si/Al ratio in Table 1\nOH: R(OH)2/Si ratio in Table 1 where R(OH)2 is hexamethonium dihydroxide\nH2O: 5 H2O in the gel formula\nHF: F−/Si ratio in Table 1 (NH4F source)\nB: Not mentioned in the recipe\nosda_names: hexamethonium dihydroxide (R(OH)2)\nosda_ratios: R(OH)2/Si ratio in Table 1\ncrystallization_temperature: 453 K (180°C)\ncrystallization_time: Time in days from Table 1, converted to hours\nproduct_names: Products column in Table 1",
    "formula abbreviations": "R(OH)2 = hexamethonium dihydroxide (structure directing agent)\nF- comes from NH4F\nSi comes from silica gel (SiO2 28.0 wt%)\nAl comes from aluminum pseudoboemite (Al2O3 69.5 wt%)\nGe comes from GeO2\nAl2O3 values need to be converted to Al values (multiply by 2 since each Al2O3 contains 2 Al atoms)",
    "ratio calculations": "For each recipe:\nSi is normalized to 1.0\nGe = 0.05 (fixed for all recipes as stated in the gel formula)\nAl = 2/(Si/Al ratio) since the ratio in the table is Si/Al and Al is from Al2O3 where 2 Al atoms per Al2O3\nOH = 2 × R(OH)2/Si (since each R(OH)2 has 2 OH groups)\nH2O = 5.0 (fixed for all recipes as stated in the gel formula)\nHF = F−/Si (direct from table)\nB = 0 (not used in recipes)\nosda_ratios = R(OH)2/Si (direct from table)\ncrystallization_time = Time(days) × 24 hours",
